Kenomine.io Design Tokens v0.1

Purpose

These tokens define the visual styling foundation for kenomine.io.

The goal is to keep the portfolio:

* clear
* calm
* editorial
* readable
* confident
* product-design focused

⸻

Color Tokens

Philosophy

Color should support clarity, not decoration.

The portfolio should feel like a clean editorial design system where the work, case studies, and diagrams remain the focus.

⸻

Neutral Colors

--color-bg: #FAFAF8;
--color-surface: #FFFFFF;
--color-surface-muted: #F3F2EF;
--color-text-primary: #171717;
--color-text-secondary: #5F5F5F;
--color-text-muted: #8A8A8A;
--color-border: #E2E0DC;
--color-border-strong: #C8C6C1;

⚠ Needs verification against current site CSS.

⸻

Accent Colors

--color-accent: #2F5D50;
--color-accent-hover: #24483E;
--color-accent-soft: #E6F0EC;

Use accent sparingly for:

* links
* active navigation
* small highlights
* selected states

Avoid using accent color for large decorative areas.

⚠ Needs definition: confirm whether green, blue, or warm neutral should be the official kenomine accent.

⸻

Semantic Colors

--color-success: #2E7D32;
--color-warning: #B26A00;
--color-error: #C62828;
--color-info: #2457A6;

Use only when showing product states, annotations, or audit notes.

⸻

Typography Tokens

Philosophy

Typography should feel editorial, calm, and highly readable.

Hierarchy should come from size, weight, spacing, and layout rather than heavy color usage.

⸻

Font Families

--font-sans: "Inter", "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
--font-serif: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
--font-mono: "SF Mono", Consolas, monospace;

Recommended:

* Sans-serif for interface and case study body
* Serif optional for editorial pull quotes
* Mono only for code, tokens, or technical references

⚠ Needs verification: confirm actual site font.

⸻

Type Scale

--font-size-xs: 0.75rem;   /* 12px */
--font-size-sm: 0.875rem;  /* 14px */
--font-size-md: 1rem;      /* 16px */
--font-size-lg: 1.125rem;  /* 18px */
--font-size-xl: 1.5rem;    /* 24px */
--font-size-2xl: 2rem;     /* 32px */
--font-size-3xl: 3rem;     /* 48px */
--font-size-4xl: 4rem;     /* 64px */

⸻

Line Height

--line-height-tight: 1.1;
--line-height-heading: 1.2;
--line-height-body: 1.6;
--line-height-caption: 1.4;

Rules:

* Use tighter line height for large headlines.
* Use generous line height for case study body copy.
* Avoid dense paragraphs.

⸻

Font Weight

--font-weight-regular: 400;
--font-weight-medium: 500;
--font-weight-semibold: 600;
--font-weight-bold: 700;

Recommendation:

Use 600 for most headings instead of overly bold weights.

⸻

Spacing Tokens

Philosophy

Spacing should create calm reading rhythm.

The site should feel spacious, not empty.

⸻

--space-0: 0;
--space-1: 0.25rem;  /* 4px */
--space-2: 0.5rem;   /* 8px */
--space-3: 0.75rem;  /* 12px */
--space-4: 1rem;     /* 16px */
--space-5: 1.5rem;   /* 24px */
--space-6: 2rem;     /* 32px */
--space-7: 3rem;     /* 48px */
--space-8: 4rem;     /* 64px */
--space-9: 6rem;     /* 96px */
--space-10: 8rem;    /* 128px */

Usage:

* 4–8px: micro spacing
* 12–16px: inline grouping
* 24–32px: component spacing
* 48–64px: section spacing
* 96–128px: major page breaks

⸻

Border Radius Tokens

Philosophy

Corners should feel modern but not overly playful.

--radius-none: 0;
--radius-sm: 4px;
--radius-md: 8px;
--radius-lg: 12px;
--radius-xl: 20px;
--radius-pill: 999px;

Usage:

* Cards: 12px
* Buttons: 999px or 8px
* Image containers: 12–20px
* Tags/chips: 999px

⚠ Needs definition: decide whether kenomine.io should use sharper editorial corners or softer product-style corners.

⸻

Shadow Tokens

Philosophy

Use shadows minimally.

Prefer borders and spacing over heavy elevation.

--shadow-sm: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
--shadow-md: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
--shadow-lg: 0 16px 48px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);

Rule:

Use shadows only for:

* cards
* overlays
* image containers
* interactive hover states

Avoid dramatic shadows.

⸻

Layout Tokens

--container-sm: 640px;
--container-md: 880px;
--container-lg: 1120px;
--container-xl: 1280px;
--content-readable: 720px;

Rules:

* Long-form case study text should stay around 640–760px wide.
* Visual artifacts can expand wider.
* Metrics and diagrams can use full-width containers.

⸻

Breakpoints

--breakpoint-sm: 480px;
--breakpoint-md: 768px;
--breakpoint-lg: 1024px;
--breakpoint-xl: 1280px;

⚠ Needs verification against current implementation.

⸻

Component Tokens

Buttons

--button-height-sm: 36px;
--button-height-md: 44px;
--button-height-lg: 52px;
--button-padding-x-sm: 16px;
--button-padding-x-md: 20px;
--button-padding-x-lg: 24px;

Button style:

* Primary: dark text or accent background
* Secondary: border only
* Tertiary: text link

⸻

Cards

--card-padding-sm: 16px;
--card-padding-md: 24px;
--card-padding-lg: 32px;
--card-radius: var(--radius-lg);
--card-border: 1px solid var(--color-border);

Use cards for:

* metrics
* project summaries
* case insights
* process steps

⸻

Tags / Pills

--tag-padding-y: 6px;
--tag-padding-x: 12px;
--tag-radius: var(--radius-pill);
--tag-font-size: var(--font-size-sm);

Use tags for:

* role
* platform
* industry
* methods
* tools

⸻

Motion Tokens

Philosophy

Motion should guide, not perform.

--duration-fast: 120ms;
--duration-base: 200ms;
--duration-slow: 320ms;
--ease-standard: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1);
--ease-enter: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.2, 1);
--ease-exit: cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 1, 1);

Use motion for:

* hover feedback
* page transitions
* image reveals
* navigation state changes

Avoid motion that delays reading.

⸻

Z-Index Tokens

--z-base: 0;
--z-sticky: 100;
--z-nav: 200;
--z-modal: 500;
--z-toast: 700;

⸻

Accessibility Rules

Minimum standards:

* Body text should be at least 16px.
* Links should not rely on color alone.
* Focus states must be visible.
* Interactive elements should be at least 44px tall.
* Text contrast should meet WCAG AA.

⚠ Add an accessibility audit checklist later.

